<title>CHINA: China firm to pay 3.7 bln yuan flood insurance.</title>
<headline>China firm to pay 3.7 bln yuan flood insurance.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The People's Insurance Company of China (PICC) is expected to pay 3.7 billion yuan ($445 million) in compensation after this year's floods in China, the Xinhua news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Severe flooding caused property losses of more than 200 billion yuan, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>PICC Property was the largest property insurer in China and now covered 85 percent of the domestic market, it said.</p>
</text>
